items: ssc-tools-raw-stacktrace
paths: file:v1/tools/cli/src/main/scala/scalascript/cli/Main.scala file:v1/tools/cli/src/main/scala/scalascript/cli/StandardMain.scala file:tests/e2e/cli-errors-are-messages.sh file:.github/workflows/ci.yml file:v1/tools/cli/src/main/scala/scalascript/cli/CliFailure.scala file:scripts/smoke-ci.ssc file:build.sbt
scope: |
  `@main def ssc` (bin/ssc-tools) has no top-level catch, so every runtime error reaches the user as
  `Exception in thread "main" java.lang.RuntimeException: ...` plus a stack trace. bin/ssc has had
  the clean `ssc: <message>` arm all along (StandardMain:19) -- the twins disagree. tests/e2e/
  v2-swift-cli.sh already asserts the ABSENCE of `Exception in thread` on nine CLI paths, so the
  repo already treats a raw trace as a defect; this generalises it to every path.
  A trace must stay REACHABLE: SSC_STACKTRACE=1 on BOTH launchers, or the fix trades a bad error
  message for an undebuggable compiler.
next: wrap the entry, mirror the hatch into StandardMain, gate both launchers
note: smoke-ci.ssc was held by 'shared-board-deletion-guard' and freed 2026-08-08; the gate registers there
